      "synthesis": {
        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": true,
        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "Compounds 1–3 were obtained by reaction of Ln(acac)3·2H2O (0.025 mmol; for 1, Gd, 0.0123 g) and H2L (0.025 mmol, 0.0068 g) in a mixed solvent of 5 mL methanol, 5 mL acetonitrile and 2 mL CH2Cl2. The solution was sealed in a 20 mL vial and heated at 70 °C for 72 h, then slowly cooled to room temperature. Yellow block-shaped crystals suitable for single-crystal X-ray diffraction were isolated. Yield 45% based on H2L for 1.",
